   "source": [
    "### Football Scouting — Zero-Shot vs One-Shot vs Few-Shot\n",
    "\n",
    "**Objective:** Compare three prompting techniques using the same fictional centre-back profile and recruitment requirements.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Results:** All three approaches classified Defender A as PRIORITY TARGET.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Zero-Shot:** The model identified the mandatory recruitment criteria and provided a detailed explanation without examples.\n",
    "\n",
    "**One-Shot:** With one example, the model maintained the classification while producing a more structured and comprehensive evaluation.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Few-Shot:** With three examples, the model maintained the classification and followed the expected output format, but generated a shorter and more generic justification.\n",
    "\n",
    "**What I learned:** Providing examples influences not only the structure of an LLM's response but also its level of detail. More examples do not necessarily improve response quality. The design and quality of the examples are as important as their quantity.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Conclusion:** For this specific scouting scenario, One-Shot produced the most informative response. However, additional player profiles and clearly defined evaluation thresholds would be necessary to determine which prompting technique performs best consistently."
   ]
